{
  "example": "`fn[load]` moves unchanged from `src/config.rs` to `src/config/load.rs`, and\nnothing else changes. `habeas refactor --map 'src/config.rs#fn[load]=src/config/load.rs#fn[load]'`\nrewrites the outline inputs that read it, recomputes the reference-set digests\nof the requirements it implements, rewrites `` `src/config.rs#fn[load]` `` in\ntheir rationales, and validation then passes without calling a model.\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.outline_inputs`\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.reference_digest`\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.rationale.addresses`\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.equivalence`",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The example describes a concrete case. `fn[load]` moves unchanged from `src/config.rs` to `src/config/load.rs`, and `habeas refactor --map` is run. The expected outcomes are that outline inputs are rewritten, reference-set digests are recomputed, rationale addresses are rewritten, and validation then passes without a model call.\n\n`tests/refactor.rs#fn[a_moved_function_keeps_its_evidence_current]` covers this scenario:\n- **Setup:** `project()` and `author()` build a project with `rules.load` and `rules.check` and current evidence for both. The test asserts that validation has no errors. `move_load` then moves `load` unchanged, and the test asserts that validation reports a stale `fn[load]` error.\n- **Command:** the test runs the real `habeas refactor --map 'src/config.rs#fn[load]=src/config/load.rs#fn[load]'` binary and asserts that it succeeds.\n- **Outline inputs:** the test asserts `record[\"inputs\"][1][\"file\"] == \"src/config/load.rs\"`. The `fn[verify]` input is unchanged. The test compares a snapshot of every other file and finds no differences.\n- **Reference digest:** the move changes the reference set of `rules.load`, because its `{impl}` moves to a new file. Validation returns no errors after the refactor, so the rewritten digest and the rewritten outline hash both match the current state. The stale state before the refactor is the contrast.\n- **Rationale addresses:** the test asserts the exact rewritten rationale. `` `src/config/load.rs#fn[load]` `` is rewritten. The prose mention of `src/config.rs` that is not an exact address is left alone and is listed for review in the report. This matches the requirement that only an exact `<file>#<selector>` code span is rewritten.\n- **Validation passes without a model:** after the refactor, `errors(root)` is empty. This check calls `habeas::validate_repository` directly, and `refactor` is only a local binary run, so no model is involved.\n- **Equivalence:** `rules.load` passed before the move and passes after it. `rules.check` reads no moved node, so the test asserts it is not reported and that its file bytes are unchanged.\n- **Idempotence:** a second run reports `Changed 0 records`.\n\nI found no assertion that contradicts the example or its cited requirements. I didn't find a behaviour the example states that the test would let through.",
  "references": "8832d7de8f757b1eab512f27090a43f6e073ba7aba1a2379baa5bf15ce0495d3",
